@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: what must be green before publishing images, and where each part runs
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
' covers: e2e/idle_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/base_template_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/ladder.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/idle.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/e2efull.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/gate.go
' covers: internal/contract/retirement_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/buildcli.go (requireRetirementLedger)
' Lineage and tags: image-lineage-and-publish.puml (same directory).
'
' ── THE RETIREMENT LEDGER BLOCKS A CLI RELEASE (N33, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ──
' A deprecated alias that promises to go "next release" needs something that
' notices the release happened. internal/contract/retirement_test.go holds a
' ledger of live retirements, each with a marker string. The four v0.2.0
' entries (two Go aliases, the egress/ run-root sweep, and the installer alias)
' were removed before the next release. The empty ledger stays active so new
' deprecations can be bounded. Tests:
'   TestEveryRetirementMarkerIsStillInTheTree  a ledger row whose marker is gone
'                                              must be deleted with it
'   TestEveryDeprecatedAliasHasARetirement     every envreg AliasOf has a row
'   TestNoRetirementOutlivesOneRelease         `git grep -F <marker> <prev>` at
'                                              the newest v* tag merged into
'                                              HEAD and not at HEAD; it fails
'                                              when that release already shipped
'                                              the marker
' A shallow clone has no tags to read, so the last test skips with a remedy.
' MEASURED, cmd/proveo-dev/buildcli.go:106,123: requireRetirementLedger runs the
' test before goreleaser on `build-cli --release` and blocks the release unless
' it PASSES — a skip blocks too. Reported: red with a marker v0.1.2 contains,
' then green.
' The gate turned red after v0.2.0 shipped. Removing the expired surfaces
' and their ledger rows made HEAD eligible for the next release.
' Why the split exists: _spec/_experiments/nested-sbx-kvm.puml — sbx is host-only.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE GATE IS IN TWO HALVES, AND THAT IS NOT A CHOICE ─────────────────────
' A proveo sandbox has docker but NOT sbx: the CLI is in no proveo image, and
' /dev/kvm does not exist there with no kvm module loaded. So the sbx-backed
' checks cannot run where the rest of them do, and a release gate that lives
' only in one place would either skip them or refuse to run.
'
' IN-SANDBOX (or any host with docker):
'   1  go build ./... && go vet ./... && go vet -tags e2e ./e2e/
'   2  go test ./...                     unit + contract
'   3  mise run build all                every image from source
'   4  mise run test-images              every TestImage* suite, hermes included —
'                                        the ONE image task; test-e2e and
'                                        test-e2e-full depend on it (N12, 2026-10-17,
'                                        MEASURED mise.toml:79,97,103;
'                                        TestOneImageTaskGatesBothReleaseGates).
'                                        HISTORY: "11 suites across all four defs",
'                                        and test-images-sbx skipped hermes.
'   5  go test -tags e2e ./e2e/          the non-sbx e2e suite
'
' ON THE HOST ONLY, because each needs sbx:
'   6  the ladder, PER DEF — one climb per target, not one climb:
'        for t in claudecode cursor opencode; do
'          PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1 PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET=$t \
'            go test -tags e2e ./e2e/ -run Ladder -v
'        done
'      claudecode is the DEFAULT target, so a bare run measures only it. The
'      sbx fixes this suite proved for claudecode were applied to cursor by
'      SYMMETRY rather than measurement — a contract with one data point.
'   7  the credential control:
'        PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT=1 PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1 \
'        go test -tags e2e ./e2e/ \
'          -run ProxyManagesTheCredential -v
'      It runs the SAME Kit twice, with and without credentials[], and fails if
'      both give the same value — so it proves the declaration CAUSES the
'      sentinel rather than merely coinciding with it.
'   8  silent-death idle, PER DEF — `mise run test-e2e-full` is this plus 6:
'        PROVEO_IDLE_TEST=1 PROVEO_IDLE_TARGETS=claudecode,cursor,opencode \
'        PROVEO_IDLE_FOR=45s go test -tags e2e ./e2e/ -run TestAgentSurvivesIdleAtPrompt
'      The ladder holds raw `sbx run`. Idle holds `proveo run`, where a leaked
'      DA1 becomes a prompt and the sandbox "was stopped". 45s is past sbx's
'      30s auto-stop and the ~14s cursor death; a SKIP is not a pass.
'
' ── THE VERDICT ITSELF IS A THING THAT CAN BE WRONG ─────────────────────────
' `ladder-all` reads the ladder's result out of `go test` output, and it has
' misread it twice, in OPPOSITE directions:
'
'   1  a SKIP exits 0, so an unchecked exit status reported PASS for four defs
'      on a host with no sbx — four climbs that never happened, certified.
'   2  the fix grepped for "--- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder" UNANCHORED, which also
'      matches the four-space-indented SUBTEST line. A def that passed every
'      rung with only its browser rung skipped was reported as not-run.
'
' Go prints the top-level result flush left and indents subtests, so the anchor
' is the whole correctness of the line. The pattern is pinned by a contract
' test as `'^--- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder [(]'`, against the two shapes verbatim
' from real runs:
'
'   ran, one rung skipped   --- PASS: TestSandboxLadder (168.93s)
'                               --- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder/2-proveo-browser-image (0.14s)
'   never ran                   ladder_test.go:314: sbx not available: sbx not on PATH
'                           --- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder (0.00s)
'
' ── THE GATE IS GO NOW (cmd/proveo-dev ladder | idle | e2e-full) ────────────
' The mise bash moved to cmd/proveo-dev (P4, _spec/_refactors/host-shell-to-go.puml);
' the column-0 anchor lives in ladder.go as a Go regexp, idle.go reads each
' `    --- PASS|FAIL|SKIP: TestAgentSurvivesIdleAtPrompt/<def>` subtest line and
' calls a def with none of the three MISS. A green subtest set under a red suite
' exit is still FAIL ("suite exit N"). gate.go tees go test output to the
' terminal while keeping the copy it reads: buffering until exit made a
' minutes-long climb look frozen for a quarter hour, and the rung logs are how
' an operator sees which layer is being exercised while it happens.
' e2e-full sets PROVEO_{IDLE,TOOLCHAIN}_TEST=1 (e2eFullEnv, MEASURED) and
' PROVEO_TEST_GO_TIMEOUT (default 150m) for the whole process, then runs the
' e2e suite, idle and the ladder in-process; every half runs, any red fails.
' PROVEO_SIGNAL_TEST=1 left the env 2026-10-16 with e2e/signal_test.go, whose
' subject — tearing down the docker egress sidecars on SIGINT — was deleted.
'
' ── WHAT A GREEN GATE DOES NOT COVER ────────────────────────────────────────
' Stated because a checklist read as complete is worse than one read as partial:
'
'   amd64.  Every measurement in this branch is arm64. `deploy` pushes
'     amd64+arm64, so the publish is the first amd64 compile. The node tarball
'     picks per-arch with a pinned sha256 for each and the purge is dpkg, so it
'     is arch-independent BY INSPECTION — which is not a build.
'
'   the first-run consent prompt. With PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT defaulted on, sbx
'     asks before injecting a service the operator has not yet bound — once per
'     service, recorded in ~/.config/sbx/credentials.yaml, and it asks even for
'     a credential it already holds. An UNATTENDED agent stops there. No test
'     covers it because it is interactive by definition.
'
'   HISTORY: TestProjectDotEnvAtEgressLayer/opencode was RED and unexplained
'     on the docker backend. It was deleted 2026-10-16 with that backend, so
'     the question it raised is closed by removal, not answered.
'
' ── HISTORY: LEAKED STATE POISONED THE RESULT, AND HID FOR HOURS ────────────
' Docker-backend era; the -egress containers and *-mitm-net networks it names
' no longer exist. The rule — match on the image, never the name — stands.
' Two proveo/opencode:local containers ran for SIX HOURS after the sessions
' that started them were killed, each holding a *-mitm-net network. They were
' invisible to `docker ps -a | grep proveo` because docker had named them
' `romantic_haibt` and `tender_rhodes` — proveo starts them without --name, so
' MATCH ON THE IMAGE, NEVER THE NAME:
'     docker ps -a --filter ancestor=proveo/opencode:local
' Removing them changed the dotenv failure from a 5m timeout to "session exited
' before a new -egress container", which is a different and more useful fault.
' The underlying defect is a teardown that does not run when a session is
' killed; cmd/proveo/clean.go exists for it and nothing invoked it.
' ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title Release gate — two halves, because sbx is host-only

node "in-sandbox · docker only" as BOX <<host>> {
  component "build + vet + go test" as GO <<app>>
  component "build all\n14 images from source" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "test-images\nevery TestImage* · hermes included\n(the one image task, N12)" as TI <<app>>
  component "e2e minus sbx" as E2E <<app>>
}

node "host only · needs sbx" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "idle × 3 defs\nproveo run · zero input" as IDLE <<db>>
  component "ladder × 3 defs\nclaudecode cursor opencode" as LAD <<db>>
  component "credential control\nsame Kit, with and without" as CRED <<db>>
}

component "deploy all\namd64 + arm64 --push" as PUB <<cloud>>
component "not covered\namd64 · consent prompt\n(the e2e never approves: SEC3)" as GAP <<error>>

GO ARROW_MAIN BUILD
BUILD ARROW_MAIN TI
TI ARROW_MAIN E2E
E2E ARROW_MAIN IDLE : hand off to the host
IDLE ARROW_MAIN LAD
LAD ARROW_MAIN CRED
CRED ARROW_MAIN PUB : only now
GAP ARROW_ERROR PUB : known blind spots

note bottom of HOST
  **Idle is the other host half.** The
  ladder holds raw ""sbx run""; idle
  holds ""proveo run"", where the DA1
  leak lives. ""test-e2e-full"" runs
  both, per def. A SKIP is not a pass.
end note

note right of LAD
  **One climb per def, not one climb.**
  The target defaults to claudecode,
  so a bare run measures a third of
  the fleet. ""test-e2e-full"" climbs
  all three, then idles all three.
end note

note bottom of LAD
  **A skip exits 0, so the verdict is grepped.**
  Unanchored it matched the indented SUBTEST line
  and called a full climb not-run; unchecked it
  called four absent climbs a pass. The pattern is
  anchored at column 0 and pinned by a test.
end note

note bottom of GAP
  **A checklist read as complete is worse than
  one read as partial.** amd64 has never been
  compiled here, and the consent prompt is
  interactive by definition.
end note

note bottom of TI
  **It prefers :local and PULLS otherwise.** A
  suite run without building first tested a
  seven-day-old published image and reported
  success — build all comes first for that
  reason, not for tidiness.
end note

note bottom of CRED
  **It proves causation, not coincidence.** The
  same Kit runs twice, with the credentials
  block and without, and an identical result
  either way fails the test.
end note

@enduml
